ss=\"name\">Doc</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">ifVersoFn</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">ifVerso </span><span class=\"fn\">ifNotVerso</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.ParserFn\">Parser.ParserFn</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.ParserFn\">Parser.ParserFn</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses as `ifVerso` if the option `doc.verso` is `true`, or as `ifNotVerso` otherwise.","docLink":"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.ifVersoFn","kind":"def","line":2236,"name":"Lean.Doc.Parser.ifVersoFn","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/DocString/Parser.lean#L2236-L2241"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.documentInfo\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Doc</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">documentInfo</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.ParserInfo\">Parser.ParserInfo</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parser information for Verso markup.\n\nListing the syntax kinds that `documentFn` produces ensures that we don't get spurious module\ndependencies.","docLink":"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.documentInfo","kind":"def","line":2220,"name":"Lean.Doc.Parser.documentInfo","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/DocString/Parser.lean#L2220-L2231"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.documentKinds\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Doc</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">documentKinds</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.SyntaxNodeKind\">SyntaxNodeKind</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The syntax kinds of the nodes that `documentFn` produces.","docLink":"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.documentKinds","kind":"def","line":2193,"name":"Lean.Doc.Parser.documentKinds","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/DocString/Parser.lean#L2193-L2218"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.locateError\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Doc</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">locateError</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">ictx</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.InputContext\">Parser.InputContext</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">pos</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String.Pos.Raw\">String.Pos.Raw</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.Error\">Parser.Error</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String.Pos.Raw\">String.Pos.Raw</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String.Pos.Raw\">String.Pos.Raw</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.Error\">Parser.Error</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the start and end of the range over which a Verso parse error at `pos` is reported, along\nwith the error to report. An end position of `none` indicates that the error has no range, but is to\nbe reported at a single point.\n\nAn error that includes an unexpected token is reported at that token's range. When such an error has\nno message of its own, as with errors from Lean's own parsers, a message is derived from the token.\n\nOtherwise, the range starts at `pos` and covers the character there, or the whole run of it when a\nVerso element repeats that character to make a single delimiter (e.g. `***` for bold text). At the\nend of the input, and at a newline, the end is `none`.\n\nWhitespace before the error stays outside the range.","docLink":"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.locateError","kind":"def","line":2158,"name":"Lean.Doc.Parser.locateError","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/DocString/Parser.lean#L2158-L2191"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.documentFn\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Doc</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">documentFn</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">blockContext</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.BlockCtxt\">BlockCtxt</a> := <a href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.BlockCtxt.mk\">{</a> <a href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.BlockCtxt.mk\">}</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.ParserFn\">Parser.ParserFn</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a document: the whitespace it starts with, then zero or more blocks.\n\nThe document's first token records the whitespace between the position where this parser starts\nand that token. A caller that starts it part-way into a larger input is responsible for the\nwhitespace before that position, which a doc comment's opening delimiter records as its trailing\nwhitespace.","docLink":"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.documentFn","kind":"def","line":2130,"name":"Lean.Doc.Parser.documentFn","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/DocString/Parser.lean#L2130-L2148"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">partial def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.blocks1Fn\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Doc</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">blocks1Fn</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.BlockCtxt\">BlockCtxt</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.ParserFn\">Parser.ParserFn</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses one or more blocks.","docLink":"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.blocks1Fn","kind":"opaque","line":2102,"name":"Lean.Doc.Parser.blocks1Fn","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/DocString/Parser.lean#L2102-L2107"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">partial def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.blocksFn\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Doc</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">blocksFn</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.BlockCtxt\">BlockCtxt</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.ParserFn\">Parser.ParserFn</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses zero or more blocks. Each block's final token consumes the whitespace that follows it, the\nnext line's indentation included, and `blockSepFallback` parses the whitespace after a block whose\nfinal token was lost to error recovery.","docLink":"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.blocksFn","kind":"opaque","line":2093,"name":"Lean.Doc.Parser.blocksFn","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/DocString/Parser.lean#L2093-L2100"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">partial def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.blockFn\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Doc</span>.<span class=\"name\">Parser</span>.<span class=\"name\">blockFn</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.BlockCtxt\">BlockCtxt</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Parser/Types.html#Lean.Parser.ParserFn\">Parser.ParserFn</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a block.\n\nWhen `recordTrailing` is set, the block's final token consumes the whitespace that follows the\nblock (including the indentation of the next line), even when error recovery lost the token that\nwould have consumed it.","docLink":"./Lean/DocString/Parser.html#Lean.Doc.Parser.blockFn","kind":"opaque","line":2029,"name":"Lean.Doc.Parser.blockFn","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/DocString/Parser.lean#L2029-L2091"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"